  "term": "sophistry",
  "definition": "Sophistry is deceptive or merely seeming reasoning, especially argument used to mislead or to leave an opponent unsure how to answer. In a narrower logical sense, it can also mean a false argument that may not actually deceive but is hard to refute.",
